its first-boot ExecStart predicate and the shipped wrapper's argv, so the tree's
rocknix-autostart.service is compared with that constant on the host (#1000).

--self-test runs root-policy subprocess controls. --payload-tests additionally
creates tiny synthetic SYSTEM/update/install payloads and release bundles using
installed filesystem tools (no distro build). Coordinator allocates these runs.
--prepare-guest-script FILE only writes a first-boot read-only serial script.
Fixtures are synthetic or public shipped defaults; no caller-supplied storage is seeded or cleaned.
